OL,3,GNEWSAKitten season hits animal rescuers
OL,4,Awith 'a bang'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn animal rescue centre is experiencing
OL,7,Fa "boom" of kittens, with the number
OL,8,Falmost doubling its usual capacity and
OL,9,Fleaving it near "breaking point", staff
OL,10,Fhave said.
OL,12,FGables in Plymouth said it had 54
OL,13,Fkittens currently in its care, with
OL,14,Fpregnant cats in care also due to give
OL,15,Fbirth soon.
OL,17,FGeneral manager Claire Sparkes said
OL,18,Fkitten season started "very late"
OL,19,Fbecause it was colder and went from
OL,20,Fwinter straight into summer without a
OL,21,Fspring.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,347,340,200,160,0,100
